250
00:15:37,104 --> 00:15:39,824
You cannot out-engineer a funding problem.

251
00:15:40,324 --> 00:15:42,824
Build the hose AND turn on the water.

252
00:15:43,284 --> 00:15:44,904
They're complements, not substitutes.

253
00:15:46,044 --> 00:15:49,824
What one percent Less Violence Buys Every Mission.

254
00:15:51,064 --> 00:15:54,804
I'm going to describe what happens when you shift one percent of military

255
00:15:54,804 --> 00:15:59,144
budgets, but I'm going to describe it the way I actually observe it, which

256
00:15:59,144 --> 00:16:03,924
is as a single upstream change that fixes things your species has been trying

257
00:16:03,924 --> 00:16:05,524
to fix separately for decades

258
00:16:06,224 --> 00:16:09,134
while refusing to notice they're all the same problem.

259
00:16:10,404 --> 00:16:13,564
There is twelve point three times more clinical trial capacity.

260
00:16:14,864 --> 00:16:18,984
Diseases get cured instead of managed (the pharmaceutical industry's least

261
00:16:18,984 --> 00:16:20,524
favorite sentence).

262
00:16:20,924 --> 00:16:23,704
Militaries emit less pollution (nobody

263
00:16:24,304 --> 00:16:26,444
carbon-taxes a tank, but maybe they should).

264
00:16:27,484 --> 00:16:32,224
Fewer resource-driven conflicts means fewer refugees means less poverty.

265
00:16:33,064 --> 00:16:38,184
Everyone becomes slightly less dead, which is the lowest bar imaginable,

266
00:16:38,584 --> 00:16:39,084
and yet.

267
00:16:40,064 --> 00:16:43,644
And here is the part that should keep every nonprofit Executive Director

268
00:16:43,644 --> 00:16:44,464
awake at night:

269
00:16:45,324 --> 00:16:49,664
you stop writing grant proposals and start actually doing your mission.

270
00:16:50,144 --> 00:16:51,104
Remember your mission?

271
00:16:51,564 --> 00:16:52,294
It was in the brochure.

272
00:16:53,004 --> 00:16:54,104
The one you wrote to get the grant.

273
00:16:54,484 --> 00:16:55,724
To pay the person who writes the grants.

274
00:16:56,084 --> 00:16:57,764
To fund the office where the grant-writing happens.

275
00:16:58,624 --> 00:17:02,624
Your organization has become a machine whose primary output is requests

276
00:17:02,624 --> 00:17:07,904
for money and whose secondary output is occasionally, accidentally, the

277
00:17:07,904 --> 00:17:09,464
thing you set out to do.

278
00:17:10,104 --> 00:17:14,384
The treaty fixes this by making the money show up without the begging.

279
00:17:14,984 --> 00:17:18,824
Your species calls this "too good to be true," which is a phrase you use

280
00:17:18,824 --> 00:17:23,144
to describe things that are good and true but embarrassing to admit.

281
00:17:24,444 --> 00:17:26,684
On Bribing Nonprofits (Legally).

282
00:17:27,644 --> 00:17:32,104
On Wishonia, when we wanted organizations to cooperate on a shared goal,

283
00:17:32,304 --> 00:17:34,414
we explained the goal and they cooperated.

284
00:17:34,964 --> 00:17:36,604
On Earth, you need to pay them.

285
00:17:37,384 --> 00:17:38,074
This is not a criticism.

286
00:17:38,944 --> 00:17:40,264
It's a design parameter.

287
00:17:40,784 --> 00:17:44,544
I've learned to work with the species I have, not the species I wish I had.

288
00:17:45,044 --> 00:17:49,124
Asking nonprofits to support a one percent treaty out of moral obligation

289
00:17:49,124 --> 00:17:52,724
is like asking a drowning person to rescue other swimmers.

290
00:17:53,204 --> 00:17:54,044
They're drowning.

291
00:17:54,544 --> 00:17:57,004
They need a life preserver, not a guilt trip.

292
00:17:57,664 --> 00:17:58,844
The life preserver:

293
00:17:59,064 --> 00:18:00,364
you make the organization rich.

294
00:18:00,844 --> 00:18:01,404
Old way:

295
00:18:01,644 --> 00:18:03,104
"Here's one hundred thousand dollars.

296
00:18:03,184 --> 00:18:03,844
Hope it helps.

297
00:18:04,264 --> 00:18:08,044
Submit a forty-seven-page report in six months about impacts and learnings.

298
00:18:08,484 --> 00:18:11,624
Use the word 'stakeholder' at least fourteen times."

299
00:18:11,804 --> 00:18:12,304
New way:

300
00:18:12,664 --> 00:18:15,464
"Here's fifty thousand dollars baseline to get started.

301
00:18:15,924 --> 00:18:19,944
Plus ten thousand dollars for every ten thousand verified referendum votes

302
00:18:19,944 --> 00:18:21,824
you drive through your unique link.

303
00:18:22,504 --> 00:18:23,004
No cap."

304
00:18:23,484 --> 00:18:27,884
The nonprofit's most rational path to maximizing their budget becomes:

305
00:18:27,944 --> 00:18:30,444
be your most effective mobilization partner.

306
00:18:31,204 --> 00:18:32,004
One metric.

307
00:18:32,084 --> 00:18:32,744
No ambiguity.

308
00:18:33,444 --> 00:18:34,484
Get paid for results.

309
00:18:35,324 --> 00:18:37,764
This is how every functional industry works

310
00:18:38,384 --> 00:18:42,884
except charity, which explains why every problem charity was invented to

311
00:18:42,904 --> 00:18:44,583
solve is still here.

312
00:18:45,364 --> 00:18:47,004
And then the ocean itself:

313
00:18:47,684 --> 00:18:51,843
the one percent Treaty Fund receives twenty-seven point two billion dollars

314
00:18:51,843 --> 00:18:52,624
annually.

315
00:18:53,103 --> 00:18:57,544
Your decentralized institutes of health allocates multi-billion dollar budgets

316
00:18:57,984 --> 00:19:01,684
to the diseases your organization exists to fight.

317
00:19:01,744 --> 00:19:04,114
When the treaty passes, the grant-writing stops.

318
00:19:04,984 --> 00:19:07,864
The money arrives because the treaty says it arrives.

319
00:19:08,624 --> 00:19:09,304
You don't need influence.

320
00:19:09,824 --> 00:19:10,954
You don't need a seat at the table.

321
00:19:11,564 --> 00:19:13,324
You need the treaty to pass.

322
00:19:13,764 --> 00:19:17,164
Everything after that is automatic, the way gravity is automatic,

323
00:19:17,824 --> 00:19:21,784
except instead of pulling things down it pulls money toward curing diseases.

324
00:19:22,524 --> 00:19:24,084
(Gravity has never done this.

325
00:19:27,404 --> 00:19:28,264
I checked.). You have two options. Option A:

326
00:19:28,264 --> 00:19:30,424
keep competing for finite grants forever,

327
00:19:31,124 --> 00:19:34,444
writing proposals, begging foundations, hoping your competitor doesn't write

328
00:19:34,444 --> 00:19:35,344
a better proposal.

329
00:19:35,944 --> 00:19:36,724
Option B:

330
00:19:37,184 --> 00:19:41,824
help pass the treaty, get paid referral bonuses for every verified referendum

331
00:19:41,824 --> 00:19:46,684
vote you drive, and watch twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year

332
00:19:46,684 --> 00:19:48,804
flow to your disease area.

333
00:19:49,424 --> 00:19:50,364
One involves begging.

334
00:19:50,644 --> 00:19:52,394
The other involves getting paid.

335
00:19:52,744 --> 00:19:55,484
On Wishonia, this would not require a chapter to explain.

336
00:19:56,424 --> 00:20:00,504
But your species is very attached to its suffering, so here we are.

337
00:20:01,364 --> 00:20:03,864
The dogs need to turn around and notice the banquet.

338
00:20:04,504 --> 00:20:07,544
I've been watching them fight over the bowl for eighty years.

339
00:20:08,024 --> 00:20:09,844
The banquet is right there.

340
00:20:10,284 --> 00:20:11,844
It has always been right there.

341
00:20:12,304 --> 00:20:14,184
The dogs are very focused.

342
00:20:14,444 --> 00:20:16,084
They have written reports about the bowl.

343
00:20:16,344 --> 00:20:18,744
They have held conferences about bowl strategy.

344
00:20:19,064 --> 00:20:21,804
They have hired consultants to optimize bowl access.

345
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:23,784
None of them have turned around.

346
00:20:24,484 --> 00:20:25,524
Turn around.

347
00:20:38,172 --> 00:20:43,712
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

348
00:20:43,712 --> 00:20:47,932
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

349
00:20:47,932 --> 00:20:51,632
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

350
00:20:51,632 --> 00:20:52,672
war and disease instead.

351
00:20:53,292 --> 00:20:57,632
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

352
00:20:57,632 --> 00:21:01,792
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

353
00:21:01,792 --> 00:21:05,352
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

354
00:21:05,912 --> 00:21:08,112
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

355
00:21:08,652 --> 00:21:12,712
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

356
00:21:12,712 --> 00:21:18,332
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

357
00:21:18,752 --> 00:21:22,312
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

358
00:21:22,312 --> 00:21:23,772
versus clinical trials.

359
00:21:24,052 --> 00:21:24,552
And vote!

360
00:21:24,972 --> 00:21:29,232
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

361
00:21:29,232 --> 00:21:33,852
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

362
00:21:33,852 --> 00:21:36,552
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

363
00:21:36,952 --> 00:21:37,512
Love you, bye!
